        "book": "Helaman",
        "chapter": 4,
        "verse": 17
      },
      {
        "text": "And it came to pass in the sixty and second year of the reign of the judges, that Moronihah could obtain no more possessions over the Lamanites.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 18,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Helaman 4:18",
        "book": "Helaman",
        "chapter": 4,
        "verse": 18
      },
      {
        "text": "Therefore they did abandon their design to obtain the remainder of their lands, for so numerous were the Lamanites that it became impossible for the Nephites to obtain more power over them; therefore Moronihah did employ all his armies in maintaining those parts which he had taken.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 19,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Helaman 4:19",
        "book": "Helaman",
        "chapter": 4,
        "verse": 19
      },
      {
        "text": "And it came to pass, because of the greatness of the number of the Lamanites the Nephites were in great fear, lest they should be overpowered, and trodden down, and slain, and destroyed.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
